{"agent":"impl-sw-baseline","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`provider` returns `swarm.merged_per_hour` and `swarm.rework_rate` without applying `[metrics] min_samples`. Given `cfg.metrics.min_samples=10` and a context with one completed work item (`first_claim=0`, `completed_at=3600`, no failed outcomes and no bugs), `_merged` returns one span and `wall=3600`, so the provider emits `value=1.0` for `swarm.merged_per_hour` and `value=0.0` for `swarm.rework_rate`. The module contract says a figure under `min_samples` merged items is `None`, so `ddflow metrics` can show a baseline from too few items.","digest":"7ed32d5acb28dd13","location":"ddflow/services/swarm_metrics.py:provider","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/swarm_metrics.py:provider"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`baseline` suppresses throughput, rework rate, and cost per item when `thin`, but leaves `critical_path` populated. Given `cfg.metrics.min_samples=10` and one merged item with `first_claim=0`, `completed_at=3600`, and `cycle_s=3600`, the result has `thin` true (`throughput.per_hour` and `rework.rate` are `None`) while `critical_path.length=1`, `critical_path.duration_s=3600.0`, `critical_path.slack_s=0.0`, and `critical_path.parallelism=1.0`. Those critical-path figures are derived from the under-sampled merged set and should be `None` under the module’s “figure under min_samples merged items is None” rule.","digest":"516fe114227c5ae1","location":"ddflow/services/swarm_metrics.py:baseline","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/swarm_metrics.py:baseline"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":16190,"diff_sha":"e1e42e03493451a687e2341018ba3d4719046878e0edc7e8b08d03b669576e76","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1073.5,"family":"alibaba","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"1125ccc76bf562cb","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/SW-baseline.rubber_duck.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261029T204648Z-ad94e048.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"51ce9a057f91a35748f85f5e5ab3afc56a257a40","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/swarm_metrics.py":"100644 a4580d5287c63a1525a33cd22f986e0689a57ab9","tests/test_swarm_metrics.py":"100644 c9b5970a6ba72dd26d9b7fa1f6cbed08d2562c85"},"reviewer":"qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/swarm_metrics.py:provider","ddflow/services/swarm_metrics.py:baseline"],"tree_sha":"51ce9a057f91+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e6351db77c690258c2ca00095","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":112951,"schema":1,"subject":"SW-baseline","ts":"2026-10-29T21:17:16.727651Z"}
